{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p5-f3221fdd","text":"Now lib/linkedin.js.

Endpoints:
- token: https://www.linkedin.com/oauth/v2/accessToken
- userinfo: https://api.linkedin.com/v2/userinfo
- register upload: https://api.linkedin.com/v2/assets?action=registerUpload
- upload PUT
- create post: https://api.linkedin.com/v2/ugcPosts

Note: ugcPosts deprecated-ish? Still operational. Alternatively use /rest/posts with LinkedIn-Version header and images API /rest/images?action=initializeUpload. Hmm. Let me think about which is more future-proof in Oct 2026.

LinkedIn v2 ugcPosts has been deprecated in docs in favor of /rest/posts, but still works for most apps. However, new apps created recently may only have access to versioned APIs. The versioned approach:

POST https://api.linkedin.com/rest/images?action=initializeUpload
Headers: Authorization, Content-Type: application/json, LinkedIn-Version: YYYYMM, X-Restli-Protocol-Version: 2.0.0
Body: {"initializeUploadRequest": {"owner": "urn:li:person:xxx"}}
Response: {"value": {"uploadUrl": "...", "image": "urn:li:image:..."}}
Then PUT binary to uploadUrl.
Then POST https://api.linkedin.com/rest/posts with body:
{
  "author": "urn:li:person:xxx",
  "commentary": "text",
