Done. Model versions are now resolved from OpenRouter's live catalog instead of being written into the code, and image generation moved off the Cloudflare worker onto OpenRouter's Image API.

## What changed

**Text model** — [lib/openrouter.js](lib/openrouter.js#L1-L9) now defaults to `openrouter/free`, OpenRouter's free-models router. It picks a zero-cost model per request and filters for models that support the request's features (structured outputs, reasoning), so the default can never rot into a retired slug. If you want a frontier model, OpenRouter ships exactly the mechanism you're describing: `~author/family-latest` aliases that always resolve to the newest release of a family. There are 19 live ones, e.g. `~anthropic/claude-sonnet-latest`, `~google/gemini-flash-latest`, `~openai/gpt-mini-latest`, `~x-ai/grok-latest`. Their compatibility contract also remaps reasoning params instead of 400-ing when the target changes, and the response's `model` field names the concrete version that answered — which `/api/cron` logs.

**Images** — [lib/image.js](lib/image.js) now calls `POST https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/images` with your same OpenRouter key. The model comes from [lib/models.js](lib/models.js): it reads `GET /api/v1/images/models` (cached six hours), drops preview/beta entries and router slugs, prefers models that accept an aspect ratio, and takes the newest. Right now that resolves to `qwen/qwen-image-2.1-turbo` (2026-10-16). `OPENROUTER_IMAGE_MODEL` pins a slug; an unknown one fails immediately listing the newest five; if the catalog is unreachable the run continues with a fallback and returns a warning. The Cloudflare worker is still there, opt-in via `IMAGE_PROVIDER=cloudflare`.

**One thing I have to correct in your plan:** `openrouter/free` cannot generate images. Its catalog entry declares `output_modalities: ["text"]`, and of the 61 image models on OpenRouter, none is free — the free tier is text only. So images cost money by design: qwen turbo is $0.0184 per image, `google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image` is $0.00003/output-token, `black-forest-labs/flux-3-image-klein` $0.008 at 768px. At one run a day that's roughly 50¢ a month. Pin a cheaper slug if you'd rather trade looks for price.

## Env changes for Vercel

Nothing new is required, and these three are optional:

```
IMAGE_PROVIDER=openrouter        # default; "cloudflare" to go back to the worker
OPENROUTER_IMAGE_MODEL=          # blank = newest in the live catalog
IMAGE_ASPECT_RATIO=16:9
```

`IMAGE_API_URL` and `IMAGE_API_KEY` are no longer required — they only apply with `IMAGE_PROVIDER=cloudflare`. If your local `.env` still sets `OPENROUTER_MODEL=google/gemini-3.8-flash` (or any concrete slug), that overrides the new default: delete the line, or switch it to a `~…-latest` alias. [.env.example](.env.example) has the full annotated set.

I also raised the function budget from 60s to 120s in [vercel.json](vercel.json) and [api/cron.js](api/cron.js), since text plus image generation moves slowly. If your plan rejects 120, set both back to 60.

